From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: isp6s: seninf: Unregister the subdev when a
 port goes

Unloading the driver oopsed in __media_entity_remove_link():

  __media_entity_remove_link+0x84/0x1d0 [mc]
  __media_entity_remove_links+0x44/0x78 [mc]
  __media_device_unregister_entity+0x90/0xf0 [mc]
  media_device_unregister_entity+0x3c/0x60 [mc]
  v4l2_device_unregister_subdev+0x8c/0xf8 [videodev]
  v4l2_async_nf_unbind_all_subdevs+0x5c/0x158 [v4l2_async]
  v4l2_async_nf_unregister+0x4c/0x88 [v4l2_async]
  seninf_remove+0x60/0xd8 [mtk_seninf6s]
  ...
  seninf_core_remove+0x64/0x130 [mtk_seninf6s]

Each SENINF port registers its subdev with v4l2_device_register_subdev()
but took it down with v4l2_async_unregister_subdev(), which does nothing
for a subdev that was not registered through v4l2-async. The port's
entity stayed in the media graph after its devm-allocated context was
freed. When two ports both link to the same CAMSV, the first port's
removal only drops its async connection to the CAMSV, so the CAMSV
keeps its links to the freed entity, and removing them when the second
port unbinds the CAMSV touches freed memory.

seninf_remove() also unregistered the subdev itself instead of leaving
the port's component, so the aggregate device kept a component whose
driver data was gone.

Unregister the subdev with v4l2_device_unregister_subdev(), which
removes its links while both ends exist, and remove the port with
component_del() so that the component framework unbinds every port
through seninf_comp_unbind() before any of them is freed.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 seninf/mtk_seninf.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/seninf/mtk_seninf.c b/seninf/mtk_seninf.c
index bb05ec7..93abfdf 100644
--- a/seninf/mtk_seninf.c
+++ b/seninf/mtk_seninf.c
@@ -2038,8 +2038,8 @@ static void unregister_subdev(struct seninf_ctx *ctx)
 
 	v4l2_async_nf_unregister(&ctx->notifier);
 	v4l2_async_nf_cleanup(&ctx->notifier);
+	v4l2_device_unregister_subdev(sd);
 	v4l2_subdev_cleanup(sd);
-	v4l2_async_unregister_subdev(sd);
 	media_entity_cleanup(&sd->entity);
 }
 
@@ -2231,7 +2231,7 @@ static void seninf_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	pm_runtime_disable(ctx->dev);
 
-	unregister_subdev(ctx);
+	component_del(dev, &seninf_comp_ops);
 
 	v4l2_ctrl_handler_free(&ctx->ctrl_handler);
 
-- 
2.55.0

